 "summary": "The Brick Colonial (Fa\u00e7ade) in real LEGO parts: the front of the brick colonial on a shallow base, at the full model's scale with the rooms behind left out. Warm taupe brick with cream sills, lintels and cornice under a gray hip roof; the entry stands forward under its pediment, the black door with its wreath under a fanlight in a cream arch between two lanterns, the arched window over it; the bay under its own little roof, white double-hung windows in pairs, and the lower wing with its dormer. In front, a lawn mown in stripes, the walk with its lamp post and mailbox, beds of boxwood, hydrangeas and arborvitae, two small round trees and a shade tree at the corner. The back is a plain wall, so it sits neatly on a shelf or against a wall.",
